[
  {"comment":"SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT. Flat faces of sheet bodies as planes (mitcad#1554): Mirror's plane, Split Body's tool, Align's plane, a sketch plane, a construction plane and an extrusion's end on a flat face of a converted and of a folded sheet, placements within 1e-6 mm. Rules t=2, r=3, K=0.3, the reference side the front. Three sheets as in cli.sheet_datums: a 40 x 20 x 2 plate converted to a sheet of one panel (F2.b0, its front at z = 2, all its faces planes); a 40 x 30 x 20 block at x = 100 converted to a U channel of its bottom and end faces (F4.b0: its bottom's wall at y = 0, the top of its wall at x = 140 at z = 20); a 60 x 20 Face at y = 50..70 folded 90 degrees up at x = 0 (F7.b0: the upright's top at z = 35 - c with c = 0.9 pi, half the fold's allowance (pi/2)(r + K t); the stationary panel's wall at y = 70). Once a bend is in a sheet, its thickness walls are B-spline surfaces, planar within 1e-6 mm, which every plane input reads as planes. The mirrored object is a 4 x 3 x 5 block at x = 60..64, y = -40..-37, z = 0..5 (F10.b0, its centre (62, -38.5, 2.5))."},
